  "problem": "A manufacturer wishes to build a cylindrical container with a base but no lid. The container must have an exact volume of $72\\pi \\,{ft}^{3}.$\nTo make the container, the manufacturer uses two materials:\n\n- a plastic sheet that costs $$1.5$ per ${ft}^{2}$ for the lateral surface,\n\n- a plastic sheet that costs $$0.5$ per ${ft}^{2}$ for the base.\n\nWhat is the radius of the container that gives the smallest manufacturing cost?",
